**/bin/
**/obj/
# Not redundant with `**/bin/`, however much it looks it. On macOS and Linux the MSBuild
# properties in .gitignore can produce directories whose NAME literally contains a backslash
# ("bin\Debug", "BuildHost-netcore"), which `**/bin/` does not match. They then enter the build
# context, MSBuild reads the backslash as an escape, and `dotnet publish` dies with a
# "MSB3552: Resource file "**/*.resx" cannot be found" that points nowhere near the real cause.
**/bin\\Debug/
**/BuildHost-*/
**/.vs/
docs/
tests/
.git/
.env
